I found an important setup issue in my split run: the entry theorem uses the loop claim coinductively, so isolating the entry by deleting the loop claim removes a required proof dependency and causes unbounded exploration. That run is not evidence against the candidate. I’m stopping that diagnostic and will select claims while retaining the complete two-claim spec context.
